WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
SPEAKER 1: That is all stated
to be in the interest of us

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.830
being ruled by our reason.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.810
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:17.560
What is the longest surviving
written constitution

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.280
in human history?

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.810
AUDIENCE: The Magna Carta?

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.720
SPEAKER 1: Students
are wonderful.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.540
AUDIENCE: I was going to
say the Ten Commandments.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.642
SPEAKER 1: Are
those constitutions?

00:00:31.642 --> 00:00:32.600
AUDIENCE: I don't know.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.985
It's an agreement between
God and the Hebrews.

00:00:37.532 --> 00:00:38.240
SPEAKER 1: Is it?

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.300
AUDIENCE: Worth a shot.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.967
SPEAKER 1: I don't
think they are the 10

00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:41.960
contractual provisions.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.400
No, the Magna Carta is
an element of the British

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.390
Constitution, it's true.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.900
But the British Constitution
doesn't come to be with that.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.548
It takes more.

00:00:56.548 --> 00:00:59.090
Oh, come on, you guys got to be
able to answer that question.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.590
AUDIENCE: The
American Constitution.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:01.710
SPEAKER 1: Ha.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:02.510
Ha.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.760
We have now named the
elephant in the room.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.320
This constitution is the
longest surviving thing

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.700
of its kind in all
of human history.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.470
And I think we've
reached why right here.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:21.510
Step 1, it gives effect to
consent to representation.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:26.310
Step 2, it locates all the
sovereignty in the people,

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.060
not in the government.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.460
No one in the government
can say that he or she is

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.120
acting of his own will, right?

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.930
Step 3, it excludes
the sovereign

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.770
from the ordinary operation of
the government, which places

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.390
a check on the sovereign too.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:51.330
And that is all stated to
be in the interest of us

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:56.580
being ruled by our reason
through discussion.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.950
James Madison was aware
that reason and speech

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.300
are the same thing.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.380
We should talk things
through before we do them.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.220
And it should not
be our passions.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.180
Passions don't tend
to last that long.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.680
Convictions do.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.910
Reason does.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:18.300
And you're arguing about it
all the time all along the way.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.890
And that means that Madison says
that these arrangements here,

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:28.750
this connection between the
people and the government

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.030
that gives power
to the government,

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:34.240
locates ultimate
authority in the people,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.560
prescribes how the people
must hold opinions over time

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.150
to make them effective--

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.040
this is a set of arrangements.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.500
What does this make it
possible for them to do?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:53.820
They can delegate the authority
to more than one place.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:59.070
You can give the legislative
power to the Congress

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:03.240
in Article I of
the Constitution.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.370
You can give the executive power
to the president in Article

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.450
II of the Constitution.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.600
They each have their
own relationship

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.730
with the sovereign people.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:22.360
They are quite equal
as regards authority.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.550
You can give all
the judicial power

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:29.600
in Article III to
the courts, and you

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.850
can use Article I and Article
II institutions to combine

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.790
to appoint the judges.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:43.200
You can leave most of the power
in the hands of the states,

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.850
and you can protect that in
Article IV of the Constitution.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.710
You see the symmetry and
the strength of that--

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:57.910
all made possible by this
consent and representation.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.130
If the sovereign was
in the government,

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.510
whatever part of
the government--

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.843
and Madison writes this over
and over in the Federalist,

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:04.780
Hamilton too--

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.180
whatever part of the government
the sovereign was in,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.120
that would become
the dominant part.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.870
Whereas now, we can
separate the powers and then

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:19.339
they can be stronger, which
you need, but still also safe.

00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:23.350
So what that means, then, is
that the principle of human

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:27.940
equality under the laws of
nature and of nature's God

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:30.430
gives rise-- and all
this happens, by the way,

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:34.450
in about eight lines in the
Declaration of Independence--

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:38.110
gives rise to the principle
of government by consent.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.090
We hold these truths
to be self-evident,

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:42.460
all men are created equal
and endowed by their creator

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:45.860
with certain inalienable rights,
among these life, liberty,

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.230
and the pursuit of happiness.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.660
To secure these
rights, governments

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.960
are instituted among men,
deriving their just powers

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.640
from the consent
of the governed.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.070
That follows from
equality up above--

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.590
under the authority
of the natural law,

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:04.090
which is just our perception of
what kind of thing each of us

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.710
is, right?

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.620
We're not like dogs.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.330
We're also,
interestingly enough,

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.630
not like god or the
angels, who aren't

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.470
mentioned in the Declaration
of Independence, right?

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.100
And so once you've got
that, then all of a sudden,

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:25.150
you lay the ground
for a government that

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:29.170
is grounded in the
people, but the powers

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:33.700
are so arranged so that the
better angels of our nature,

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.420
to quote Lincoln,
drive the government.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:42.910
And that, the claim by the
founders and the claim by me,

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:45.640
they believe, the founders
believed, that this government,

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.880
because it's in accord
with human nature, which

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:55.660
is that nature above the beast
and below God, this government

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.420
can last a long time--

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.470
in principle, as long as the
Earth lasts or people last.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:07.143
And it has lasted a long time.

00:06:07.143 --> 00:06:08.560
SPEAKER 2: Thank
you for watching.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.530
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlights series

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.440
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.640
online courses.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.500
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

